# Manifest Log — append-only completion tracking
# Format: TIMESTAMP | TASK_ID | PHASE | ROLE | field=value ... | narrative
# 
# This file is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for project state.
# Every entry is immediately committed to git after writing.
#
# Phase values (closed enum — no ad-hoc values):
#   TASK_REGISTERED  — task created (orchestrator/team-arch)
#   CLAIMED          — worker began a task
#   CODE_WRITTEN     — worker's toolchain loop passed; readiness signal, not completion
#   REVIEW_REQUESTED — team-arch detected CODE_WRITTEN, spawning SecArch
#   REVIEW_PASSED    — SecArch approved (may include CONDITION_OPEN entries)
#   REVIEW_FAILED    — SecArch rejected (findings file committed)
#   ISSUES_FOUND     — team-arch re-queuing after REVIEW_FAILED or TESTER_FAILED
#   TESTER_ASSIGNED  — team-arch spawning Tester after REVIEW_PASSED
#   VERIFIED         — Tester confirmed PASS or PASS_WITH_WARNINGS
#   TESTER_FAILED    — Tester found failures (report file committed)
#   DONE             — orchestrator/team-arch confirmed VERIFIED; only path is through VERIFIED
#   BLOCKED          — worker exhausted 3 toolchain cycles without passing
#   REARCHITECT      — orchestrator closed task; successor registered separately or descoped
#   CONDITION_OPEN   — SecArch raised a condition (one entry per condition)
#   CONDITION_CLOSED — condition remediated (one entry per condition)
#   ESCALATED        — retry budget exhausted, user notified
#   SHIPPED          — Phase 6 complete, project delivered
#   TEAM_SHIPPED     — all charter tasks complete, team workflow finished
#   ASSUMPTION_LOGGED — role hit a judgment call, picked lowest-risk default
#
# Role values: orchestrator | worker | secarch | tester | team-arch-<N>
#
# ── STATUS DISCIPLINE (do not violate) ────────────────────────────────────────
# PHASE must be EXACTLY one of the values above. Never write free text, and never
# write a future-tense action, as a PHASE or as a standalone entry.
#
# This log records ONLY state transitions that have ALREADY HAPPENED. It is not a
# plan and not a scratchpad. Planning notes, intended next steps, and in-progress
# reasoning go in `.agent-project/notes.md`.
#
# Why this rule exists: a run once ended with the final manifest line reading
# "applying conditions as cleanup commit, then push, then copy to toolkit". That was
# an intention, never executed — but it is structurally indistinguishable from a
# completion record, so the abandoned run looked mid-flight for six days and four
# security conditions went unremediated. A future-tense note in this file is a defect.
#
# ── STATUS OWNERSHIP (no role writes its own terminal state) ──────────────────
# Workers write CODE_WRITTEN, not DONE. SecArch writes REVIEW_PASSED/REVIEW_FAILED.
# Tester writes VERIFIED/TESTER_FAILED. Orchestrator is the only writer of DONE.
# See roles/manifest-schema.md for the full state machine and invariants.
#
# ── MACHINE-CHECKABLE INVARIANTS ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are greppable from git history with no in-context knowledge. Check them
# before SHIPPED or TEAM_SHIPPED:
#
#   1. Every registered task is done or rearchitected:
#      reg=$(grep -c '| TASK_REGISTERED |' manifest.log)
#      done_n=$(grep -c '| DONE |' manifest.log)
#      rearch_n=$(grep -c '| REARCHITECT |' manifest.log)
#      [ "$((done_n + rearch_n))" -eq "$reg" ]
#
#   2. Every DONE has a preceding VERIFIED for the same task_id:
#      (enforced at Phase 6 ship gate — a DONE without VERIFIED blocks shipping)
#
#   3. Every raised condition is closed:
#      [ "$(grep -c '| CONDITION_OPEN |' manifest.log)" -eq "$(grep -c '| CONDITION_CLOSED |' manifest.log)" ]
#
#   4. A run with DONE entries and no SHIPPED entry is ABANDONED, not in progress.
#      Startup checks this before creating a new project (see SKILL.md Startup).
#
# Entry shapes for paired statuses:
#   <timestamp> | <task_id> | TASK_REGISTERED | orchestrator | title=<title> | depends_on=<ids|none> | <description>
#   <timestamp> | <task_id> | CONDITION_OPEN  | secarch | <condition_id> | <description>
#   <timestamp> | <task_id> | CONDITION_CLOSED | worker | <condition_id>
#
# Recovery: If a session dies, read this log + git log to reconstruct state.
# Rule: Never merge a branch whose task has no DONE entry here.
# Rule: Every write to this file is followed by: git add + git commit
#
